Exception: the source files under tests/smhasher3/ are NOT covered by the
above. SMHasher3's framework is licensed under the GNU General Public
License, either version 3 or (at your option) any later version. The two
patch files modify SMHasher3's own sources, and the adapter is written
against SMHasher3's headers and macros and exists only to be compiled into
that program. Conservatively, all three are GPL-3.0-or-later. Each carries
an SPDX identifier, and the license text is in tests/smhasher3/COPYING.

The affected files are:

  tests/smhasher3/hayahash.cpp
  tests/smhasher3/0001-macos-size_t-reference-binding.patch
  tests/smhasher3/0002-cmake-detect-apple-silicon-as-arm.patch

This does not affect hayahash64 itself. Everything else in this repository,
including the reference implementation hayahash.h and every language port,
is public domain under the Unlicense above, and the adapter's including of
hayahash.h does not change that header's license. SMHasher3 is fetched at
test time and is not part of any release artifact; building it locally does
not affect the license of this software, though redistributing the
resulting combined SMHasher3 executable must comply with the GPL.
